# The demonstration harness appends its local audit trail beside itself, one JSON object
# per line. It is a run artifact, not source: it carries pseudonymised identity
# references and stage records from whatever question was asked, and a commit offering it
# would be a commit offering somebody's message history. Nothing ignored it until
# 2026-08-20, so any run left it staged and waiting to be added by mistake.
apps/telegram-bot/demo-audit.jsonl
apps/telegram-bot/*.jsonl
# The same argument for a redirected console. `run.py` prints the question, the stage counts and
# the operator's own lines; until 2026-08-21 it printed the credential **path** as well. A
# redirection inside the tree left that file waiting to be added by mistake, exactly as the audit
# trail was before it was ignored.
apps/telegram-bot/*.log

# O diario de corridas: registro do que rodou NESTA maquina, nao fato sobre o codigo.
apps/telegram-bot/runs/

# A chave da service account do BigQuery: mora aqui, NUNCA no git -- igual ao .env.
apps/telegram-bot/bigquery-service-account.json

# operational audit archive of the steward CLI (T110/D-13) — runs/ of any cwd
runs/
docs/estado-das-nove-frentes.txt
docs/progresso-do-projeto.md
docs/analise-dimensional-013.md

# uv.lock de qualquer diretorio: byproduto de `uv run`, nunca conteudo do repo.
# MEDIDO em 2026-09-04: zero uv.lock rastreado (`git ls-files | grep uv.lock` vazio), e o
# `packages/semantic_catalog/uv.lock` deixado por um agente ja barrou um push hoje -- ele CAI
# sob os prefixos vigiados das duas travessias, e o de `apps/telegram-bot/` NAO cai sob nenhum.
# A regra e a mesma para os dois porque a diferenca e acidente de onde o comando rodou.
uv.lock
